# Everything is ignored by default. The film folders sitting beside this file
# hold a few hundred megabytes of JPEGs and carry arbitrary human names, so an
# allow-list is the only rule that stays safe when a new one appears.
*

!.gitignore
!.nojekyll
!README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!requirements.txt
!ocr_subs.py
!words.txt

# the page
!index.html
!favicon.svg
!app.css
!app.js
!worker-py.js
!coi-serviceworker.js
!langs.json
!vendor/
!vendor/**

# tessdata/ is the command line's own copy, and is mostly symlinks into
# /usr/share that would break on any other machine. The browser's copy of the
# language data lives in vendor/tessdata/ and is committed.
